/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  Freestream U = (268.83, 0, 0) m/s (M=0.79, freestream_conditions.py).
  highlightInlet represents captured mass flow (reference_data.
  MASS_FLOW_RATIO = 0.71) leaving the external domain into the unmodeled
  engine: mdot = mfr*rho*V_inf*A_highlight = 18.447481306189033 kg/s.

  Originally a fixedValue (190.87 0 0) — a fully-constrained velocity
  vector at a patch immersed in the flow domain (not a domain edge) —
  which is the prime suspect for the severe iteration-1 pressure blowup
  seen across every solver attempt (p swinging +275525/-750791 Pa vs an
  ambient of 66829.5 Pa) even after fixing fvSchemes term names, the
  SIMPLE/SIMPLEC relaxation mismatch, and the waveTransmissive p BC.
  Switched to flowRateInletVelocity, matching OpenFOAM's own
  compressible/rhoPorousSimpleFoam/angledDuct tutorial pattern, which
  lets the solver relax the velocity magnitude via the pressure-correction
  loop instead of hard-pinning it.

  Sign convention (confirmed from that tutorial's 0.orig/U + 0.orig/p:
  the flowRateInletVelocity patch there is paired with p type zeroGradient,
  exactly like highlightInlet's p already is): flowRateInletVelocity
  builds U as (massFlowRate / (rho*A)) directed AGAINST the patch's
  outward normal, i.e. positive massFlowRate always means flow entering
  the domain. highlightInlet's outward normal points downstream (+x, out
  of this domain into the engine) and the captured flow must LEAVE
  through it, so massFlowRate must be NEGATIVE here to reverse that
  convention into an outflow.

  This alone did not fix it: switching from fixedValue to a full-strength
  flowRateInletVelocity from iteration 1 reproduced the same severe
  first-iteration pressure blowup (p ~+270000/-750000 Pa vs an ambient of
  66829.5 Pa) seen with fixedValue, and regenerating the mesh with
  tightened snappyHexMeshDict quality controls (targeting the 1803
  concave cells checkMesh flagged) did not change it either -- ruling out
  both the highlightInlet BC type and mesh conditioning as the driver.
  massFlowRate is a Function1<scalar> (confirmed in
  flowRateInletVelocityFvPatchVectorField.C), so it can be RAMPED natively
  within one continuous run via OpenFOAM's scale+linearRamp composition
  (see tutorials/multiphase/potentialFreeSurfaceFoam/oscillatingBox for
  the pattern) -- letting the exterior freestream field establish over
  the first 200 iterations before the capture sink reaches full strength,
  rather than imposing it at full strength against a still-uniform
  initial field.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       volVectorField;
    object      U;
}

dimensions      [0 1 -1 0 0 0 0];

internalField   uniform (268.83 0 0);

boundaryField
{
    farFieldInlet
    {
        type            freestreamVelocity;
        freestreamValue uniform (268.83 0 0);
        value           uniform (268.83 0 0);
    }
    farFieldOutlet
    {
        type            freestreamVelocity;
        freestreamValue uniform (268.83 0 0);
        value           uniform (268.83 0 0);
    }
    farFieldSide
    {
        type            freestreamVelocity;
        freestreamValue uniform (268.83 0 0);
        value           uniform (268.83 0 0);
    }
    cowlAndAfterbody
    {
        type            noSlip;
    }
    highlightInlet
    {
        type            flowRateInletVelocity;
        massFlowRate
        {
            type    scale;
            value   -18.447481306189033;
            scale   { type linearRamp; start 0; duration 200; }
        }
        value           uniform (190.87 0 0);
    }
}

